WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.390
- You know my next guest.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.223
I know you do.

00:00:02.223 --> 00:00:05.620
She has sold over 40
million albums worldwide.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.310
Her song "The Boy is Mine"

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.710
is one of the biggest singles in history.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:11.190
Now she's back with a new album.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.220
It's called B7 and it's out now.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.080
Here she is, Brandy!

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.570
- Hey, Kels! (laughs)

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.440
- Hi!

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.050
I love you!

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.920
- I love you, Kelly Clarkson.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:22.753
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:22.753 --> 00:00:24.500
I literally was sitting
here talking to my friend

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.800
and sitting here and I was like,

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.660
oh my gosh. I used to jam,
like, to your records,

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.040
like all the way to volleyball games.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.106
I'd have my Walkman, I'd be like,

00:00:32.106 --> 00:00:33.976
♪ Sitting up in my room ♪

00:00:33.976 --> 00:00:34.970
- Come on!

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.450
- I think that you are so great!

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:37.677
What an amazing career.
- Thank you.

00:00:37.677 --> 00:00:39.090
And like not only your hits,

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.930
but other hits you've written for people

00:00:40.930 --> 00:00:42.980
like as a writer, you're just insane.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.020
But how are you?

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.500
Like how's the family, how's quarantine?

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.860
How's everything?

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.693
- It's been...

00:00:47.693 --> 00:00:49.820
It's been crazy, such
a crazy time, you know?

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.750
But I feel like my family and I,

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.270
we've been, you know, a lot closer.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.080
You know, I've been
blessed to have my parents

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.330
here with me, my daughter.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:00.950
So we've just been spending a
lot of quality time together.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.500
- So your new song, "Baby Mama,"

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.250
first of all, I love the
video, I love the song,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.960
but it's dedicated to
your daughter, right?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.793
So how is-
- It is.

00:01:06.793 --> 00:01:08.250
- [Brandy] It's dedicated to my daughter.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.707
- Yeah, and was she excited about that

00:01:09.707 --> 00:01:11.440
and the fact that you got
Chance the Rapper on it?

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.380
That's amazing.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:13.570
- Super, super excited.

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:16.010
You know, I had to get
my mommy points for that,

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:17.610
you know, just doing a song about her,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.140
about my unconditional love for her,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.100
and then just a shout out to
all the single moms out there

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.268
who have it tough, you know,
raising their families,

00:01:25.268 --> 00:01:27.100
and Chance the Rapper,

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.910
being as though he's such
an amazing, amazing talent.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.809
And getting him on board
- Yeah.

00:01:31.809 --> 00:01:33.730
was a great collaboration.

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:36.070
I'm so thankful that he
got on board with that.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:36.903
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:38.270
Yes, it was great.

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:40.960
So the new album is your
first in eight years.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.010
So I mean, first of all took a minute,

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.000
but like, so what does it mean to you

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.580
to actually finally get to release this?

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:48.680
Do you feel like you've been working on it

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:49.513
for quite some time,

00:01:49.513 --> 00:01:52.180
just kind of evolving like how
it's gonna end up sounding?

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.013
- I do.

00:01:53.013 --> 00:01:55.020
I feel like this is a
very special album for me

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.410
because it's taken so long

00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:58.630
and because it's so personal for me.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.170
I got a chance to write a lot
of the songs on this album

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.510
and just really take my
time to craft a body of work

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.210
that I can really be proud of.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.440
So I just hope the fans
really connect to it

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:08.910
and relate to it.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.460
- Oh, I'm sure, I'm sure they will.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:12.420
You have, I mean, I'm just
gonna keep doting on you,

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.420
but you have literally the
coolest tone of any singer.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:20.180
Like it's, it's so incredible.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.900
It's the perfect amount of
like pure, but like raw,

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.220
and like raspy and, and just soulful.

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:26.320
It's so good.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.940
I just, and I remember
like when I was a kid,

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:31.300
I was so excited because I loved you,

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.380
I loved Whitney Houston, and
y'all both did "Cinderella."

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.840
So I found out this story though
that you, way before this,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.320
is this true that you
literally snuck backstage

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.570
to meet her before you were famous?

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:44.510
- I definitely did.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.440
I was in the nosebleed
section of her concert

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.330
and I talked my way all the way backstage.

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:50.500
I told everybody,

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.600
all the ushers that I
was gonna pay their bills

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.820
'cause one day I was gonna
famous and they believed me

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.450
and I talked my way all the way backstage,

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.720
but by the time I got back there,

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.810
she was gone and that broke my heart.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.370
But I met her later on

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.830
and I got a chance to do so
many amazing things with her

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.140
and create a beautiful friendship.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.920
And I miss her to this day, so.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.753
- Yeah.

00:03:10.753 --> 00:03:13.050
I mean, and what an amazing
thing too, like, I can...

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.810
I'm with you in the sense
of like some of that

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:16.990
just inspired me as a vocalist as well.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:19.910
I also heard that Miss Diana
Ross gave you some advice.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.170
I love your life, by the way.

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.140
I'm like, life is awesome!

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.950
So where, it was when you
were coming up, right,

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:26.940
that she gave you some advice?

00:03:26.940 --> 00:03:27.773
What was that?

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:28.606
- Yeah.

00:03:28.606 --> 00:03:29.439
She gave me a lot of cool advice.

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:31.250
Number one, I was chewing
gum a lot at the time

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:32.800
when we worked together and she told me

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:35.180
I need to close my mouth
when I'm chewing gum,

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.870
she told me I need to make sure the powder

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.560
that I use on my face matched my neck.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.400
Of course.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.330
And then she also told me to
give everything that I do 100%.

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.760
You know, she's such a beautiful, poised,

00:03:46.760 --> 00:03:48.910
classy, you know, timeless artist.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.770
And, you know, I always
wanted to, you know,

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.130
follow in her footsteps in that way.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.070
Just such a great example and, you know,

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:56.100
shout out to Miss Ross,
I love her very much,

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.250
and just had the pleasure
of working with her.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.630
- Yeah, she just like, you know,

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.843
when you think of like what
the definition of like a lady,

00:04:01.843 --> 00:04:04.160
like a true lady.
- Yes, she is.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.600
- Such a lady, such grace.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.400
- Yeah, I know!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:09.233
I love that.

00:04:09.233 --> 00:04:11.560
I'm a big fan of hers as
well and her daughter.

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.270
But so when are we finally going to see

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.450
a "Moesha" reboot, okay?

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.650
We see all these reboots and
I was such a "Moesha" fan.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.430
When is this happening?

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.550
- You know what?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.940
We're still talking about it.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.550
I'm so open for it, I want it so badly,

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.420
and I think just the way the show ended,

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:29.550
it ended on a cliffhanger,
and I think, you know,

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:31.820
the people that have supported
"Moesha" over the years,

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.410
they want answers.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:36.414
And I feel like it would be
so appropriate to do one.

00:04:36.414 --> 00:04:39.940
And I just want everybody
that's watching, I'm with it.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.510
I really want to do it.
- Yeah.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.700
- So is there a young singer actress

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.240
you could see starring in this?

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.690
Like taking on your part in "Moesha?"

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.320
- I don't want to give my part up.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.610
I want to do the reboot. (laughs)

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:53.600
- I love it, I love it.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.175
I didn't know if you'd
reboot it in a different way.

00:04:55.175 --> 00:04:56.820
You know how people keep
rebooting in a different way

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.120
and they almost take like a different role

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.070
and like somebody else comes up?

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.240
I didn't know how y'all would do that.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.870
But that's cool!

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.550
You're like me, you like
a lot of jobs. (laughs)

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.383
- I love to act.

00:05:05.383 --> 00:05:08.800
I love acting, and I just would
love to just tell that story

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.330
and see how far I could go.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:11.163
- Yeah.

00:05:11.163 --> 00:05:12.840
Well, it is great to see you.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.320
I'm literally, I'm such a big fan.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.430
I really wish we could have
done this in my real studio

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.700
'cause I want to do nothing
but give you a giant hug

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:21.360
and say thank you from the
girl that played volleyball,

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.290
like growing up listening
to all of your music.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.510
And I think that even now,
like I love "Baby Mama,"

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:27.700
I love all, I love your texture,

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.920
I love your like attack on a song,

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.140
I think, and I thought it
was really interesting.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:32.973
And as a songwriter,

00:05:32.973 --> 00:05:35.410
I really enjoyed just
being inspired by you.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.755
So thank you.
- Thank you so much.

00:05:36.755 --> 00:05:37.588
- You know what?

00:05:37.588 --> 00:05:38.421
I feel the same way about you.

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:40.730
My daughter told me to
tell you that she loves you

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:43.560
and just, we love you and support you,

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.050
and congratulations on your show

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.120
and everything that you're doing.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:49.120
You're such an inspiration,
Kelly, honestly.

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:50.470
- Oh, thank you so much!

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.193
Well tell her I said hey!
- You're welcome.

00:05:52.193 --> 00:05:53.026
- I will.

00:05:53.026 --> 00:05:54.170
- And hey, everybody,

00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:56.300
Brandy's latest album B7 is out right now.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.403
You got to go get it.

